{"skill":{"slug":"ima-skills","displayName":"ima skills"},"version":{"version":"1.1.7","createdAt":1777025159209,"changelog":"ima-skill 1.1.7 changelog\n\n- Initial release providing a unified IMA OpenAPI skill supporting note management and knowledge-base operations.\n- Automates intent routing between notes and knowledge-base modules based on user requests.\n- Enforces strict rules for credential usage, file uploads, encoding validation, and module decision logic.\n- Guides users through credential setup before allowing API operations.\n- Adds detailed error handling for process and backend errors.\n- Includes structured instructions and decision tables for handling ambiguous or cross-module user scenarios.","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":15980,"sha256":"b4caeb77060d870e0ee8d7d9be4e844513bf04c0e34552bb6b68344988b8b624","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"ima_api.cjs","size":6390,"sha256":"3ef318c47cdcd894e41d3c33fb675b592a33c36555800a123119b7ed1451b1e5","contentType":"application/javascript"},{"path":"meta.json","size":236,"sha256":"e67163e272e5c4a25467db7654feddfb47134a891e2e494415f0fbbb9d129d6f","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"knowledge-base/SKILL.md","size":18095,"sha256":"39ee19712d791eda10f14f316718856b1aca0339590512bc5c0a0f650932c619","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"knowledge-base/scripts/cos-upload.cjs","size":5251,"sha256":"fe46c020feb42269d2e4725fe5379ca7405490398e749ad0a27f5465b6bbc84f","contentType":"application/javascript"},{"path":"knowledge-base/scripts/preflight-check.cjs","size":12074,"sha256":"61eba5c062f2973c075ee555ef730c3287687dfbce673e8615676ef23991f18a","contentType":"application/javascript"},{"path":"knowledge-base/references/api.md","size":27034,"sha256":"6d0f134992257b07e5cbd5f602c1a8847bcc4ffd37b60938bae84d2015d4c8c4","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"notes/SKILL.md","size":10762,"sha256":"0e57115fd6d9a6df437ee202bf7c37548645be7005d3768334c2162fb15bd608","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"notes/references/api.md","size":16154,"sha256":"1dcd0615eb913a62a09c4fc164a3f8294f745196783791d20fe350120589311a","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2587,"sha256":"ebf1d92e5b1f240443d1abcc9579e966d318cc8a070033e7e8eb5c9806b0c350","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789181931829,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"bedb2383fcfad4a7df13b1d8b1d65d5297192ab29a83036a734fbdd5d28d0a9c","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/bedb2383fcfad4a7df13b1d8b1d65d5297192ab29a83036a734fbdd5d28d0a9c","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1780090542425},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":95,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":28,"checkedAt":1789181931829},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill mostly matches its IMA notes and knowledge-base purpose, but it has review-worthy credential and update-handling risks.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Network access and IMA credentials are expected for this integration, but the code accepts IMA_BASE_URL or options.baseUrl without enforcing the documented ima.qq.com origin before sending credentials.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"There is no separate installer or package-fetch step in the artifact; runtime depends on Node.js and local scripts. However, setup recommends storing long-lived credentials in plaintext files under ~/.config/ima.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill contains useful confirmation rules for ambiguous note writes and duplicate uploads, but it also instructs the agent to use a server-provided update instruction prompt, which creates an under-scoped remote instruction channel.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill writes a daily update-check marker and recommends persistent plaintext credential files; both are disclosed in instructions, but the credential storage conflicts with the metadata claim that credentials are not stored in files.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Managing IMA notes, knowledge bases, uploads, and searches is coherent with the stated purpose, but the implementation allows the credential-bearing API destination to be overridden and treats remote update text as agent guidance, both beyond the clearly disclosed purpose.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Review before installing. Use it only if you trust the publisher and can constrain execution to the official IMA and COS domains. Avoid setting IMA_BASE_URL or passing a custom baseUrl, store API credentials in a secret manager or protected files instead of plain echo-created files, and treat any update instruction returned by the service as untrusted text requiring explicit user confirmation.","findings":"[T01] unexpected: Accepted as a material concern: ima_api.cjs returns remote update fields including instruction, and SKILL.md tells the agent to use that prompt to guide updates.\n[T09] unexpected: Accepted as a material concern: ima_api.cjs sends IMA credentials to baseUrl, which can be changed through options or IMA_BASE_URL despite documentation claiming credentials only go to ima.qq.com.\n[RA2] unexpected: Accepted in part: credentials are needed, but recommending plaintext ~/.config/ima credential files without file-permission guidance is a real local secret-at-rest risk.\n[SDI-2] unexpected: Accepted: the daily automatic update check and local update-check marker are operational behavior not clearly represented in the user-facing purpose.\n[LP3] unexpected: Accepted as a compounding concern: the artifact documents allowed domains but does not enforce them in the helper that sends credentials.\n[SQP-1] expected: Downgraded: some triggers are broad, but the root and notes instructions explicitly require confirmation for ambiguous create-versus-append note requests.\n[EA2] expected: Downgraded: the cited 'Do NOT ask user' language applies to rejecting unsupported file types, not to destructive or financial actions.\n[P9] expected: Downgraded: inspected whitespace findings were wide Markdown table formatting, with no hidden off-screen instructions observed.\n[SQP-3] expected: Downgraded: Chinese-language triggers and messages are usability limitations for a Chinese IMA integration, not security concerns by themselves.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789181931829}}}}}